  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - A SNARE complex consists of several membrane bound proteins that vesicle membrane
    fusion depends on.
  - SNARE complex is activated by calcium ions, also the product of the GLP1-R signaling
    cascade.
  - Calcium triggers plasma membrane-bound and vesicle-bound SNARE components to
    interact and intertwine.
  - The two phospholipid bilayers are pulled together, merging and forming a hole
    to allow material exchange.
